      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Determine the value of $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{5}).$",
      "original_html_sha256": "9869ba2ee885c0ff9f316bbaec00720787040f0f09d916c8693db9a5d19eca76",
      "extractor_sha256": "af03036879151d6bc1d8a980c3dbf01d042d978e39d96a25bdfe63cd50ef1a10",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980995/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/9869ba2ee885c0ff9f316bbaec00720787040f0f09d916c8693db9a5d19eca76.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The binomial coefficient $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{r})=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $n=7$ and $r=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{5}) & =\\frac{7!}{(7-5)!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5!}{2!\\cdot 5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{2\\cdot \\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{2} \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "7f3da9077289beaecf02cd43c02f82e320a31e0c44f9614d7e75fef9b226a832",
